  "limits": [
    "Span, row and identity framing are observations of these stock artifacts. The cited upstream code does not define their internal field semantics.",
    "Exact substring checks leave partial matches, transformed representations and relationships between decoded settings open.",
    "This evidence contains no calibration settings or proprietary row payloads and makes no claim about runtime selection or active controller state."
  ],
  "method": [
    "Read matching installed files and group PTBs by exact file content. SHA-256 identifies each byte sequence.",
    "Split each PTB at half its file length. Verify the aligned 24-byte prefixes and use the repeated leading byte sequence 0 to 4 to verify fixed-width row locations in both spans. The two zero-byte offsets in the prefix are span-relative.",
    "Read the three little-endian 32-bit region lengths at image offsets 20, 44 and 68. The configuration region starts after the 256-byte header and the first two regions and extends to end of file.",
    "Verify both configuration tags and use the byte at region offset 91 to bound a printable ASCII identity beginning at offset 92 and ending in NUL. Compare bytes before the second tag within and across the observed chip steppings.",
    "For each indicated pair, test exact substring equality at any byte offset using Python bytes containment. Count pairs once even if a match occurs at multiple offsets."
  ],
